ADVANCED EXCEL NOTES

1. ADVANCED FORMULAS

Advanced formulas Excel mein data ko calculate, search aur analyze karne ke liye use hote hain.

Important functions:
• IF – condition check karna
• AND – multiple conditions check karna
• OR – alternative conditions check karna
• SUMIF / SUMIFS – condition ke according total
• COUNTIF / COUNTIFS – condition ke according counting
• AVERAGEIF / AVERAGEIFS – condition ke according average
• IFERROR – errors ko handle karna 

Example:
=IF(B2>=40,"Pass","Fail")

2. LOOKUP FUNCTIONS

Lookup functions ka use kisi table mein information search karne ke liye hota hai.

Important functions:
• VLOOKUP
• HLOOKUP
• XLOOKUP
• INDEX
• MATCH

VLOOKUP vertical data mein search karta hai.
HLOOKUP horizontal data mein search karta hai.
XLOOKUP modern aur flexible lookup function hai.
INDEX + MATCH advanced lookup ke liye commonly use hota hai.

3. DATA SORTING AND FILTERING

Sorting data ko particular order mein arrange karta hai.

Types:
• A to Z
• Z to A
• Smallest to Largest
• Largest to Smallest

Filtering ka use sirf required data ko display karne ke liye hota hai.

Example:
Sirf Delhi ki sales show karna.

4. CONDITIONAL FORMATTING

Conditional Formatting conditions ke according cells ko automatically format karta hai.

Uses:
• Low marks highlight karna
• Duplicate values find karna
• Top/Bottom values highlight karna
• Data Bars
• Color Scales
• Icon Sets

Path:
Home → Conditional Formatting

5. DATA VALIDATION

Data Validation ka use incorrect data entry ko prevent karne ke liye hota hai.

Uses:
• Dropdown list
• Number restrictions
• Date restrictions
• Text length restrictions

Example:
Department column mein sirf HR, IT, Sales select karna.

6. EXCEL TABLES

Excel Table data ko structured format mein organize karta hai.

Advantages:
• Automatic formatting
• Automatic filtering
• Structured references
• Automatic formula filling
• Easy data management

Shortcut:
Ctrl + T

7. PIVOT TABLE

Pivot Table large data ko quickly summarize aur analyze karta hai.

Isse hum:
• Total sales
• Average sales
• Product-wise sales
• Region-wise sales
• Month-wise sales

calculate kar sakte hain.

Main areas:
• Rows
• Columns
• Values
• Filters

8. PIVOT CHART

Pivot Chart Pivot Table ke data ko graphical form mein represent karta hai.

Common charts:
• Column
• Bar
• Line
• Pie

Reports aur dashboards mein iska use hota hai.

9. SLICERS

Slicer Pivot Table ya Table ko visually filter karne ka tool hai.

Example:
Region slicer mein Delhi select karne par sirf Delhi ka data show hoga.

Slicer dashboards ko interactive banata hai.

10. POWER QUERY

Power Query Excel ka powerful data cleaning aur transformation tool hai.

Uses:
• Data import
• Data cleaning
• Duplicate removal
• Blank values handling
• Columns split/merge
• Data type change
• Multiple files combine
• Tables merge

Path:
Data → Get & Transform Data

11. WHAT-IF ANALYSIS

What-If Analysis different situations ke results ko analyze karta hai.

Main tools:
• Goal Seek
• Scenario Manager
• Data Table

Example:
Required profit achieve karne ke liye kitni sales chahiye.

12. GOAL SEEK

Goal Seek required output ke basis par input value find karta hai.

Example:
Agar target profit ₹50,000 hai, to required sales find karna.

Path:
Data → What-If Analysis → Goal Seek

